# Pinned downloads of deploy/bootstrap.sh that scripts/fetch-model.sh does not already pin (the embedder, the
# reranker and the GGUFs are pinned there by repository revision and sha256). Sourced by bootstrap.sh; one VAR=value per
# line, no spaces around '='. Nothing on the box updates itself: changing a pin is an edit here and a rerun.
#
# The release bundle is pinned by the commit sha given to bootstrap.sh (and its .sha256 next to it on the release);
# the corpus snapshot is the operator's file (--snapshot, optionally --snapshot-sha256).

# llama.cpp, the llama-server that serves the cpu rung (trevor-llama.service runs /usr/local/bin/llama-server).
# b11146 is the build every CPU number in design/trevor-self-contained-deploy.md section 5 was measured with
# (`llama-server --version` on the development machine: build 11146, commit 7fe450e19), released 2026-09-23. It has
# the flags the units use (--no-repack, --poll, --cache-ram, --no-webui). The Ubuntu x64 CPU archive loads the best
# CPU backend (AVX2, AVX-512) at run time. The sha256 is GitHub's asset digest for this file, read from
# https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tags/b11146 on 2026-10-19 (16,998,357 bytes, not
# downloaded here). To move the pin: change all three lines together, take the sha256 from the release's asset digest
# or from sha256sum of a copy you trust; bootstrap.sh refuses an empty or mismatching sha256.
LLAMA_CPP_TAG=b11146
LLAMA_CPP_ASSET=llama-b11146-bin-ubuntu-x64.tar.gz
LLAMA_CPP_SHA256=c150306eb16b5ab696f76a8bdf810c35fd98a24e82158742e6fa28f420ff8410
LLAMA_CPP_BASE_URL=https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download
